+# TASK-260830-1x524u — Shared Runtime Story revalidation
+
+## Verdict
+
+Not landing-ready and not handed off to review. Product/runtime validation is green, but the required `story_final` Change Request was not published and repository/board landing gates remain unresolved. No product source was edited by this tester run.
+
+## Exact candidate and dependencies
+
+- Candidate branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260715-1y04r0`.
+- Freshly fetched base: local `main` and `origin/main` both `b3422b05226253a17676b9b84c764071fe3dbe74`.
+- Candidate: local and remote Story refs both `dc41c1b7629d92606657d2757c83747a85b79d09`.
+- Merge base: `b3422b05226253a17676b9b84c764071fe3dbe74`; ahead/behind versus main: `5/0`; candidate tree: `f17349ef3060b2eaf39903bcc790b3fd2cf7c896`.
+- Managed worktree was clean before and after validation. Five prior Change Requests are `checkpointed`; no final-task Change Request exists.
+- All eleven prior Story children are terminal `done`; this task is the only active child.
+- Direct blockers `STORY-260715-jnpbyz`, `STORY-260715-lkshfz`, and `TASK-260715-nphtib` are `done`. Their required architecture/SSH inputs and the nested blockers queried for M0 bindings are also `done`.
+- Board projection reports `isBlocked=false`. The Story is advisory-blocked only by downstream Stories that depend on this Story; those are not hard landing blockers.
+
+## Reproduced gates
+
+| Gate | Result | Evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `make validate-core` | exit 0 | Boundary/native/libssh2 checks passed; 514 tests in 44 suites passed; build passed. The 25 declared known issues are the explicitly unavailable, non-selected ReluxNIOSSH adapter rows. |
+| Eight focused runtime suites | all exit 0 | `RuntimeMessageCodecTests`, `TunnelRuntimeCoordinatorTests`, `ProviderAdapterContractTests`, `VPNSessionControllerTests`, `M1RuntimeCompositionTests`, `MacOSProductionRuntimeOwnershipTests`, `RuntimeDiagnosticsTests`, `SSHBootstrapErrorMappingTests`. |
+| `make m1-runtime-harness-test` | exit 0 | 6 tests passed; 7/7 deterministic fixtures passed. Repeated privacy-boundary run also exited 0. |
+| `make m0-bindings-check m0-bindings-test` | exit 0 | `productionCompositionPermitted=true`; 32 tests passed, including narrowed, missing, malformed, drifted, duplicate, and production-call-site rejection shapes. |
+| Adapter builds | both exit 0 | `ReluxTunnelIOSAdapter` and `ReluxTunnelMacOSAdapter`. This compiles shared roots only; it does not claim iOS production availability. |
+| `make macos-targets-validate` | exit 0 | Unsigned macOS Debug/Release host/provider builds, generated provider graph, and relay-resource contract passed. No installation, signing, provider launch, or VPN activation. |
+| Documentation and diagram | corrected run exit 0 | PlantUML syntax passed; four task-scoped SVG renders are byte-identical to checked-in artefacts; required files exist; `git diff --check` passed; worktree stayed clean. The first shell attempt exited 127 after a zsh special `$path` variable was overwritten; the corrected full rerun passed. |
+| Board validation | process exit 0, semantic issue present | `task-board validate` printed one `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH`: `EPIC-260715-3810we` remains `backlog` while its child aggregate is `development`. A zero process exit is not treated as a green semantic result. |
+
+## Negative evidence and production call sites
+
+- The production M0 binding entry point rejected absent evidence, malformed-as-unknown evidence, a narrowed two-of-three gate, rebound upstream evidence, repository pin drift, dependency-closure widening, and selected libssh2 patch/header/license drift.
+- `M1RuntimeCompositionTests` drove the production dependency factory and proved that graph construction is not reached before exact manifest validation; it also distinguishes absent from unreadable manifests.
+- Runtime/provider tests rejected unknown or stale snapshots, malformed and future commands, duplicate/concurrent provider failures, sensitive diagnostic values, high-cardinality labels, and narrower repetition bounds.
+- The checked-in production call site `App/ReluxProxyMacTunnel/Sources/PacketTunnelProvider.swift` remains a lifecycle shell: `startTunnel` returns success and does not instantiate `MacOSProviderCompositionRoot`. Documentation states this limitation explicitly. Therefore no live-provider-wiring claim is made.
+
+## No system mutation boundary
+
+- Overall pre/post hashes for NetworkExtension configurations and DNS state matched exactly; the Relux process set remained empty (`count=0`).
+- The raw `netstat -rn` hash changed and is reported as inconclusive because that output includes dynamic fields. It is not used as proof either way.
+- A normalized route-topology projection (destination, gateway, flags, interface), NetworkExtension configuration hash, DNS hash, and Relux process-set hash were captured before and after a fresh representative harness run. All four matched exactly and the harness exited 0.
+- Commands were limited to SwiftPM tests/builds, deterministic harness execution, unsigned Xcode builds, source/diagram checks, board reads/writes, and read-only `scutil`/`netstat` observations. No command installed or launched a provider, invoked `startVPNTunnel`, changed routes, or changed DNS.
+
+## Landing blockers and recovery
+
+1. Current run `RUN-260830-b09219` was launched while `TASK-260830-1x524u` was classified `metadata`; its immutable run manifest has no Story/worktree binding, so its completion cannot invoke the managed-workspace Change Request publisher. The task class was corrected to `code` for a successor run, but a `story_final` Change Request for this task is still absent.
+2. Read of `task-board.config.json` succeeded, but it contains no `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` configuration (`rg` exit 1). The integration contract refuses landing when the suite is unconfigured.
+3. Four Story checkpoint commits have a good signature status (`G`), but `2f0d30c1369fd2440173f8537d8d6b2ec232c075` is unsigned (`N`). This tester will not rewrite shared Story history.
+4. Board validation reports the Epic/Story parent-status mismatch described above.
+
+Recovery is internal rework, not a human product decision: rerun a tester producer after the completed `code` classification correction so it binds to the same Story workspace; configure the exact landing validation suite without overwriting the user's existing `task-board.config.json` changes; repair/review the unsigned checkpoint using the commit-owning workflow; correct the parent aggregate mismatch; then publish and independently review the resulting `story_final` Change Request. Re-run branch/OID, system-state, and validation checks against the new exact candidate.
